<b>א.</b> (Taz sk 2:) Rather [the verse speaks of] alacrity itself: “Let him strengthen himself like a lion” means that the moment he awakens from sleep he should rise; “and let him be the one who awakens the dawn” means he should accustom himself to light foods and the like so as not to sleep much and to arise before dawn—for “strengthening” does not apply while asleep; accordingly it should have said “and let him [be],” not “let him be…” [but the wording teaches habituation—see context].
